:: Crossroads_Midnight_Start [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:thummansala_banyan_wind #audio:monsoon_light #haptic:heartbeat_slow #vignette:0.55]
The bottle-dynamo rubbing against your front bicycle tire whines once and goes black as the rusted chain jumps the rear sprocket. Your wheels grind to a halt in the loose red laterite gravel of the Thummansala—the deserted three-way junction where the Anuradhapura tank-bund track forks toward the village cremation ground.

It is 11:52 PM. Overhead, the curtain of aerial banyan roots hangs dead still in the suffocating dry-zone night. Out in the thorn-scrub, a nightjar clicks like a wooden rattle, and the sudden vacuum presses against your eardrums like {mutate: "the warm breath of the dry tank wind" -> "a twelve-foot giant holding its breath six paces behind your rear mudguard" @2500}.

[[Whistle a loud baila tune into the dark to steady your nerves while fitting the greasy chain->Gravel_Meat_Parcel][$taboo_whistled_crossroads = true, $balma += 20]]
[[Crouch in strict silence and keep your left thumb pressed against the iron Giraya cutter in your pocket->Banyan_Root_Culvert][$tanikama += 10]]


:: Gravel_Meat_Parcel [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:thummansala_banyan_wind #audio:ceb_power_cut #haptic:dread_throb #vignette:0.64 #balma:10]
Your whistle dies flat against the banyan trunks without throwing back a single echo from the water. Swinging from your handlebar in a brown newspaper parcel is half a pound of roasted wild boar curry from your uncle's almsgiving house—carried without a sliver of lime or cold iron to seal the smell.

Warm boar fat has soaked translucent through the Tamil newsprint. As your knuckles turn black with chain grease, a sudden downdraft reeking of {mutate: "crushed palu leaves and dry tank silt" -> "turned cemetery clay, wet wood-ash, and singed boar bristles" @2300} sweeps across the three-way fork.

[[Leave the roasted boar parcel unwarded in the basket and look toward the approaching lantern->Culvert_Pilgrim_Lantern][$taboo_carried_uncovered_meat = true, $balma += 15]]
[[Slide your forged iron betel-cutter inside the newspaper twine to ward the meat->Shattered_Charnel_Pot][@anchor_held $balma -= 5]]


:: Banyan_Root_Culvert [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:thummansala_banyan_wind #audio:monsoon_light #haptic:heartbeat_slow #vignette:0.58]
Working by touch alone, you roll the oily chain back onto the iron teeth without making a sound. Strapped to your rear carrier rack is a warm banana-leaf parcel of spiced wild boar meat from the village dane.

Directly beneath your pedals, inside the dry concrete storm-culvert that cuts under the three-way junction, dead leaves scrape violently against the cement—as if something with shoulders far too broad for a three-foot pipe is {mutate: "a rock-python coiling in the dry silt" -> "dragging a caved-in left collarbone along the rough concrete" @2400}.

[[Call out to the dim kerosene lantern bobbing down the temple track->Culvert_Pilgrim_Lantern][$taboo_whistled_crossroads = true, $balma += 15]]
[[Mount the pedals and ride hard without warding the meat parcel on your carrier->Shattered_Charnel_Pot][$taboo_carried_uncovered_meat = true, $balma += 15, $tanikama += 10]]
[[Lock your thumb on the iron Giraya cutter and wheel the bicycle silently past the culvert->Shattered_Charnel_Pot][@anchor_held $balma -= 5]]


:: Culvert_Pilgrim_Lantern [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:thummansala_banyan_wind #audio:ceb_power_cut #haptic:heartbeat_slow #vignette:0.66]
Down the third arm of the junction comes a tall, gaunt figure draped in an unbleached white Upasaka sarong, holding a soot-blackened kuppi bottle-lamp at hip level. The wick burns with a sputtering, bile-green flame that smells of rancid margosa oil and grave tallow.

His chin is tucked so low into his chest that you cannot see his throat, yet his flared nostrils twitch audibly toward your handlebar: {mutate: "Are you riding back to the wewa village so late, malli?" -> "Unwrap the roasted boar flesh on your iron frame and hand it into the dark." @2050}.

[[Fall into step beside the lantern-bearer toward the center of the crossroads->Backwards_Shadow_Stride][$balma += 15]]
[[Grip the cold iron Giraya in your pocket and veer wide around him->Shattered_Charnel_Pot][@anchor_held $balma -= 5]]
[[Untie the warm boar-meat parcel and take the green kuppi-lamp from his hand->Outcome_Athura_Biso_Kotuwa_Pilgrim][$taboo_carried_uncovered_meat = true, $balma += 45]]


:: Backwards_Shadow_Stride [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:sohon_boar_silhouette #audio:ceb_power_cut #haptic:heartbeat_panic #vignette:0.76 #balma:15]
As the green kuppi-lamp swings six inches above the red laterite dust, your eyes drop to the pilgrim's bare feet. With every stride he takes forward toward the tank bund, his cracked heels point ahead while his ten ash-grey toes point backward toward the cremation ground—and his left shoulder caves four inches lower than his right.

Before you can recoil, he blows the bottle-lamp out with a wet snort. Against the pale trunk of the banyan tree, his shadow rears {mutate: "six feet tall in the starlight" -> "twelve cubits into the upper canopy with the curved white tusks of a wild boar" @1850}.

[[Wrench your handlebars away and sprint toward the center of the fork->Shattered_Charnel_Pot][$tanikama += 15]]


:: Shattered_Charnel_Pot [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:sohon_boar_silhouette #audio:ceb_power_cut #haptic:heartbeat_slow #vignette:0.68]
Right at the dead center of the three-way fork lies a smashed red-clay Bindum Muttiya pot left behind from a midnight exorcism. Spilled cremation ash, burnt lime Riti bark, and tarnished copper coins form a pale chalk line across the tire ruts.

Beyond the pot, the gravel track climbs the steep earthen embankment of the Wewa tank bund. In the starlight, the white wood-ash in the middle of the road swirls without wind into {mutate: "a drift of dry lime powder" -> "a colossal five-fingered handprint pointing straight toward your left shoulder blade" @2200}.

[[Kick the clay pot-shards out of your way and roll your tires straight through the ritual ash->Tank_Bund_Footsteps][$taboo_stepped_ash_pot = true, $balma += 25]]
[[Push the bicycle under the low-hanging banyan roots on the verge to bypass the ash->Banyan_Root_Noose][$tanikama += 10]]
[[Hold the cold iron Giraya and score a protective iron line across the gravel->Cemetery_Boundary_Stone][@anchor_held $balma -= 5]]


:: Banyan_Root_Noose [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:thummansala_banyan_wind #audio:ceb_power_cut #haptic:dread_throb #vignette:0.74 #balma:10]
You duck your shoulders beneath the dense curtain of aerial banyan roots bordering the ditch. Instead of dry bark, the hanging tendrils feel warm, muscular, and slick with black charnel grease.

A fibrous root as thick as a well-rope loops across your windpipe in the dark—drawing taut as {mutate: "your shirt collar snags on a low branch" -> "five unseen, soot-blackened fingers twist the root against your jugular" @2000}.

[[Claw at the tightening root with your bare nails and tear free onto the bund->Tank_Bund_Footsteps][$balma += 15]]
[[Press the razor edge of the iron Giraya cutter against the root until it recoils->Tank_Bund_Footsteps][@anchor_held $balma -= 10]]


:: Tank_Bund_Footsteps [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:sohon_boar_silhouette #audio:ceb_power_cut #haptic:dread_throb #vignette:0.76 #balma:10]
You heave the heavy steel bicycle up the earthen slope of the tank bund. To your left, black reservoir water laps against the ancient granite rip-rap; to your right, the rusted barbed-wire fence of the village Susāna Bhūmiya cremation ground leans into the chest-high iluk grass.

Four yards behind your rear mudguard, a dead palu limb as thick as a man's thigh snaps with the report of a shotgun. Heavy, lopsided footsteps—one stride crushing the gravel, the next dragging a crippled heel—thunder up the slope behind you, and a hot, bristling snort stirs the hair at your nape: {mutate: "It is only a stray water-buffalo climbing the bund" -> "Turn your neck and see how Gothaimbara set the boar's head backwards on my spine" @2000}.

[[Whip your chin around over your left shoulder to see what is behind your wheel->Boar_Tusk_Apparition][$taboo_looked_back_snap = true, $balma += 20]]
[[Keep your neck rigid and look down toward the black water of the sluice gate instead->Sluice_Gate_Splash][$tanikama += 10]]
[[Lock your eyes straight ahead on the bund crown and crush the iron Giraya in your fist->Cemetery_Boundary_Stone][@anchor_held $balma -= 10]]


:: Sluice_Gate_Splash [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:sohon_boar_silhouette #audio:arterial_pulse #haptic:dread_throb #vignette:0.78 #balma:10]
Down by the ancient granite Biso Kotuwa sluice tower, the black tank water erupts in a violent, churning wave—as though a carcass the weight of an elephant had just been dropped from the sky.

Crawling up the stone steps through the crushed lotus reeds comes the suffocating stench of wet cremation ash and {mutate: "decaying tank weeds" -> "a giant, boar-snouted silhouette climbing the embankment on all fours" @2000}.

[[Force your legs forward toward the whitewashed cemetery boundary pillar->Cemetery_Boundary_Stone][$balma += 10]]


:: Boar_Tusk_Apparition [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:sohon_boar_silhouette #audio:yak_bera_ritual #haptic:heartbeat_panic #vignette:0.82 #balma:10]
You twist your neck—and look straight into a bristling, mud-caked snout rearing twelve cubits into the banyan canopy. Grey steam jets from flared nostrils that smell of scorched marrow and split arecanut. Its head sits turned one hundred and eighty degrees backward upon a neck as thick as a palmyra trunk, and a grinding, subterranean laugh rattles from its throat: {mutate: "A wild sounder rooting in the cemetery ditch" -> "Jayasena has found a new spine to bear the mark of Gothaimbara's toe!" @1950}.

[[Throw your weight onto the pedals and race toward the boundary stone->Charnel_Gassima_Jolt][$balma += 15]]
[[Plant your boots in the gravel and hold the forged iron Giraya before your face->Cemetery_Boundary_Stone][@anchor_held $balma -= 10]]


:: Cemetery_Boundary_Stone [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:sohon_boar_silhouette #audio:yak_bera_ritual #haptic:heartbeat_panic #vignette:0.80]
At the corner of the cemetery fence stands the four-foot whitewashed Sohon Kanuva boundary stone. Squatting atop the narrow masonry pillar—yet towering sixteen feet into the night—is a colossal form plastered in grey human ash, its left shoulder stove inward from the warrior Gothaimbara's kick, crowned with the wet, tusked head of a wild boar.

In its right fist it squeezes a pale ash-gourd shaped like a human torso, drinking the red lime-sap that runs between its knuckles. The air turns thick with dummala smoke as {mutate: "the night wind bends the banyan limbs" -> "the cemetery titan raises an open, soot-blackened five-fingered palm high above your left shoulder blade" @1950}.

[[Bellow a curse into the dark and swing your iron bicycle pump at the shadow->Charnel_Gassima_Jolt][$taboo_cursed_boar_shadow = true, $balma += 25]]
[[Tuck your chin, clamp your thumb over the iron Giraya, and back away without turning your spine->Charnel_Gassima_Jolt][@anchor_held $balma -= 15]]


:: Charnel_Gassima_Jolt [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:sohon_boar_silhouette #audio:arterial_pulse #haptic:dread_throb #vignette:0.84 #balma:10]
A silent, concussive shockwave—the Charnel Gassīma—detonates at the base of your skull and rips down your vertebrae. The horizon of the tank bund tilts forty-five degrees into the black water, and every night-insect in Anuradhapura goes simultaneously mute. Behind your left scapula, the night air congeals into freezing tallow: {mutate: "Your tire skidded on the loose laterite slope" -> "Mahasona has measured the span between your shoulder blades for his seal" @2000}.

[[Fling your arms wide to catch your balance as your spine locks rigid->Shoulder_Ash_Strike][$balma += 20]]
[[Crush the cold-iron arecanut cutter against your sternum and whisper the Gothaimbara warrant->Shoulder_Ash_Strike][@anchor_held $balma -= 15]]


:: Shoulder_Ash_Strike [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:iron_betel_cutter_ash #audio:arterial_pulse #haptic:heartbeat_panic #vignette:0.86 #balma:15]
The moonless sky above the tank bund drops like a quarry slab. Before your lungs can draw air, a freezing, sledgehammer blow slams squarely between your shoulder blades—not the strike of knuckles, but the impact of a wet sack of cemetery ash dropped from thirty feet overhead.

You pitch face-first into the red gravel beside the twisted bicycle frame. Your cervical spine locks solid, your teeth chatter until the enamel chips, and the boar-headed shadow blots out the stars above your back: {mutate: "You merely struck your shoulder against the iron handlebar" -> "My five fingers are branded in indelible charnel soot across your flesh!" @1900}.

[[Grind the forged iron Giraya into your breastbone and spit three times onto the gravel->Outcome_Athura_Mahasona_Survived][@anchor_held $balma -= 30]]
[[Collapse across the spoked wheel as the freezing ague paralyzes your diaphragm->Outcome_Athura_Mahasona_Struck][$balma += 40]]
[[Wrench your stiffened neck around in the dirt to stare straight up into the boar's tusks->Outcome_Athura_Backwards_Cervical][$taboo_looked_back_snap = true, $balma += 45]]


:: Outcome_Athura_Mahasona_Survived [#samayam:ALUYA_DAWN #flow:iron_betel_cutter_ash #audio:monsoon_light #haptic:iron_grip #vignette:0.34]
The cold steel of the Giraya betel-cutter bites into your palm, grounding the shockwave before it can enter your heart. A furious, guttural boar-snort shears a branch from the overhanging banyan tree, pelting the gravel with dry twigs, before retreating into the cemetery mist as the temple bell tolls for the Aluya dawn watch.

When you wheel your bent bicycle into your compound at daybreak, the back of your white cotton shirt is scorched with a five-fingered print of grey ash—yet the skin beneath is unmarked.

[[Examine the crossroads case from the Kattadiya exorcist perspective->Kattadiya_Mahasona_Entry][$tanikama = 40]]
[[Relive the midnight ride at the Thummansala crossroads->Crossroads_Midnight_Start][$balma = 20, $tanikama = 50]]


:: Outcome_Athura_Mahasona_Struck [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:sohon_boar_silhouette #audio:yak_bera_ritual #haptic:dread_throb #vignette:0.90]
The spinal shockwave snuffs out your vision like a pinched wick. When tank-fishermen find you beside the three-way culvert at dawn, you are curled rigid in the red gravel, convulsing with an ice-cold ague that three wool blankets cannot warm.

When your elders cut away your torn shirt, a stark, five-fingered handprint of greasy black cremation soot—the Anguru Atha—is stamped deep into the flesh over your left shoulder blade. A bicycle runner is dispatched immediately with a Bulath Hurulla sheaf to summon a master of the Mahasona Samayama.

[[Accept the Bulath Hurulla summons and step into the Kattadiya role->Kattadiya_Mahasona_Entry][$tanikama = 80]]
[[Return to the Anuradhapura crossroads at 11:52 PM->Crossroads_Midnight_Start][$balma = 20, $tanikama = 50]]


:: Kattadiya_Mahasona_Entry [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:dummala_vidiya_cards #audio:monsoon_light #haptic:iron_grip #vignette:0.46]
You enter the sandy Anuradhapura compound at nightfall as the tall bamboo Vidiya pavilion is lashed together with gokkola palm strips. Inside the house, the young man shivers so violently that the wooden bed-frame rattles against the lime wall, his neck locked forty degrees to the right.

His uncle kneels and places the Bulath Hurulla sheaf beside your brass pahana lamp. Before touching the boar-tusked Kōlama mask, you draw the top betel leaf and hold its blade against the golden flame.

[[Pass the Pahana flame behind the betel leaf to read the five crossroads Lakunu->Sastra_Mahasona_Leaf_Check][$tanikama -= 5]]
[[Lift the patient's shawl to inspect the black five-fingered handprint first->Patient_Handprint_Forensics][$tanikama -= 5]]


:: Sastra_Mahasona_Leaf_Check [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:iron_betel_cutter_ash #audio:ceb_power_cut #haptic:heartbeat_slow #vignette:0.52]
Through the backlit betel blade, the charnel signatures stand out in stark relief: an ash-grey bruise at the leaf tip from whistling at the midnight Thummansala; a knotted left vein where roasted boar meat was carried unwarded; a central tear where he looked back on the tank bund; a greasy soot-sheen across the right veins from trampling the Bindum Muttiya ash pot; and a charred petiole stem from defying the cemetery boundary stone.

The diagnosis is absolute: {mutate: "he has merely contracted marsh-fever from the tank reeds" -> "Mahasona has stamped the five-fingered Anguru Atha warrant upon his spine" @2200}. Solemn terror only swells the Cemetery Titan's stature—to shrink him and break the spinal shock, you must stage the comic Kōlama card duel and blind him with Dummala resin fire.

[[Verify the physical handprint on the patient's left shoulder blade->Patient_Handprint_Forensics][$balma += 5]]
[[Step into the torchlit sand arena to deal the rigged Thovil card game->Thovil_Card_Duel_Prep][$balma += 10]]


:: Patient_Handprint_Forensics [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:sohon_boar_silhouette #audio:ceb_power_cut #haptic:heartbeat_slow #vignette:0.58]
You peel back the wool shawl from the boy's left scapula. Stamped deep beneath the epidermis—impossible to scrub away with lime juice or soap—are five splayed, giant finger-marks of greasy black cremation soot.

Whether struck by the headless duelist avatar Jayasena Yaka or the boar-snouted Maha Sohona, whispered prayers alone will fail. In the therapeutic psychodrama of the Thovil, the paralyzed victim must hear the entire village laugh aloud at the demon's humiliation until his mortal terror shatters.

[[Summon the yak bera drummer and spread the mat for the Thovil card duel->Thovil_Card_Duel_Prep][$tanikama -= 10]]
[[Return to the brass pahana to re-verify the betel leaf veins->Sastra_Mahasona_Leaf_Check][$tanikama -= 5]]


:: Thovil_Card_Duel_Prep [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:dummala_vidiya_cards #audio:yak_bera_ritual #haptic:iron_grip #vignette:0.56]
The yak bera drums pivot from a funeral thunder into a sharp, syncopated comic banter. Wearing the bristling wild-boar mask of Mahasona, your dancer lumbers into the sand arena roaring for raw human blood—only for the drummer to mock his backwards-turned neck and challenge him to a rigged game of cards (Kola Sellama) for stale rice-cakes.

To strip the titan of his terror and unlock the boy's spine, you must win three consecutive comic trumps on the mat—answering his Boar, Charnel Ash, and Crossroads boasts with Gothaimbara's Little Toe, the Iron Giraya, and the Dawn Rooster's Crow—and then hurl the Pandama torch upward against his wind to ignite the Dummala fire-cloud.

[[Win the three comic card trumps and swipe the torch upward to ignite the Dummala flare->Midnight_Gothaimbara_Varama][$balma += 10]]


:: Midnight_Gothaimbara_Varama [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:dummala_vidiya_cards #audio:yak_bera_ritual #haptic:heartbeat_panic #vignette:0.82 #balma:15]
A blinding mushroom of powdered Dummala resin fire roars twenty feet into the Anuradhapura night! Outlined against the rolling orange fireball, the boar-headed shadow trips over the edge of the card mat as the watching villagers—and the shivering boy on the verandah—erupt into cathartic, fearless laughter.

Furious at his public humiliation, Mahasona makes one final, ground-shaking lunge toward the verandah posts to reclaim his warrant: {mutate: "The cemetery giant will bring the roof beams down upon your head!" -> "By the left toe of the warrior Gothaimbara, your boar-head sits backwards and your warrant is ash!" @2000}. Lock the cold iron Giraya under your thumb and strike the Gothaimbara Varama cadence!

[[Hold the iron Giraya, recite the Gothaimbara Varama, and cleave the clay ash-pot->Outcome_Kattadiya_Mahasona_Banished][@anchor_held $balma = 0]]
[[Strike the clay pot without anchoring the cold iron Giraya ward->Outcome_Kattadiya_Mahasona_Backfire][$balma += 35]]


:: Outcome_Kattadiya_Mahasona_Banished [#samayam:ALUYA_DAWN #flow:iron_betel_cutter_ash #audio:monsoon_light #haptic:iron_grip #vignette:0.30]
With the forged iron Giraya locked under your thumb, you thunder the ancient verses of Jayasena's decapitation at the hands of Gothaimbara and bring the blade down across the clay Bindum Muttiya pot. Stripped of his dread by the crowd's laughter and bound by the warrior's warrant, the towering boar-shadow shrinks into a harmless wisp of grey woodsmoke that drifts away across the tank water.

On the verandah, the black five-fingered Anguru Atha stain fades from the boy's shoulder like drying mist. He turns his neck freely and laughs aloud as the dawn breeze stirs the banyan leaves.

[[Replay Casefile 04 from the midnight crossroads in Anuradhapura->Crossroads_Midnight_Start][$balma = 20, $tanikama = 50]]
[[Examine a new Bulath Hurulla summons sheaf in Kattadiya Mode->Kattadiya_Mahasona_Entry][$balma = 25]]


:: Outcome_Kattadiya_Mahasona_Backfire [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:sohon_boar_silhouette #audio:yak_bera_ritual #haptic:dread_throb #vignette:0.88]
Your thumb slips from the iron Giraya as you cast the Dummala resin. Instead of erupting upward, the resin backfires in a choking black cloud of soot that snuffs out the courtyard torches, freezing the villagers' laughter in their throats.

In the sudden pitch dark, lopsided footsteps thunder across the sand toward the verandah.

[[Relight the Pandama torch and deal the Thovil card duel again->Thovil_Card_Duel_Prep][$balma = 40]]
[[Pull the scorching boar-tusked Kolama mask tighter over your face to confront the shadow->Outcome_Kattadiya_Boar_Mask_Fused][$balma += 35]]


:: Outcome_Athura_Backwards_Cervical [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:sohon_boar_silhouette #audio:yak_bera_ritual #haptic:heartbeat_panic #vignette:0.92]
As you force your chin around against the freezing lock in your vertebrae, a dry crack echoes across the tank water—not the sound of a broken cord, but the ancient seal of Gothaimbara resetting Jayasena's head.

At six in the morning, villagers watching the tank bund scream and drop their baskets. You are walking steadily down the red gravel path—yet {mutate: "your head is bowed in exhaustion" -> "your chin rests squarely between your shoulder blades, your open eyes staring permanently backward at the three-way crossroads while your heels walk forward into the cemetery scrub" @2000}.

[[Come to a halt at the 11:52 PM crossroads again->Crossroads_Midnight_Start][$balma = 25, $tanikama = 55]]


:: Outcome_Athura_Biso_Kotuwa_Pilgrim [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:thummansala_banyan_wind #audio:yak_bera_ritual #haptic:dread_throb #vignette:0.92]
The gaunt pilgrim accepts the warm newspaper parcel of boar curry with a low, wet grunt—and presses the soot-blackened kuppi bottle-lamp into your grease-stained fingers. Instantly, the brass base of the lamp welds itself to your palm.

At dawn, your rusted bicycle is found leaning empty against the cemetery stone. And the next night at 11:52 PM, when another lone rider halts at the Thummansala with a slipped chain, {mutate: "the road is empty under the banyan roots" -> "it is you who walks out of the culvert mist carrying the green-flamed bottle-lamp on backward-pointing, ash-crusted toes" @2050}.

[[Come to a halt at the 11:52 PM crossroads again->Crossroads_Midnight_Start][$balma = 25, $tanikama = 55]]


:: Outcome_Kattadiya_Boar_Mask_Fused [#samayam:MADDHAMA_MIDNIGHT #flow:sohon_boar_silhouette #audio:yak_bera_ritual #haptic:dread_throb #vignette:0.94]
Boiling dummala pitch coats the inside of the carved Kaduru-wood mask. When you try to tear the mask off your face, there is no seam left between the painted wood and your cheekbones.

Course black bristles erupt along your jaw as the carved wooden tusks root deep into your gums. With a single concussive jolt, {mutate: "you stumble onto the sand mat" -> "your left collarbone caves four inches inward, your neck twists backward toward the stars, and you lumber out of the compound on all fours toward the cremation ground" @2000}.

[[Replay Casefile 04 from the midnight crossroads in Anuradhapura->Crossroads_Midnight_Start][$balma = 20, $tanikama = 50]]
[[Re-enter Kattadiya Triage from the beginning->Kattadiya_Mahasona_Entry][$balma = 25]]
